<main>

    <h1>T1a07-Decision - Jordan</h1>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>About Decision Making</h2>

        <div class="assignment">
            <b>JavaScript If Statements</b>

            <p>
                Decision making allows JavaScript to run different
                code depending on whether a condition is true or false.
                This page demonstrates simple if statements,
                if...else statements, and complex conditions.
            </p>
        </div>

        <p>
            Enter a number and test the examples below.
        </p>

        <p>
            Reference:
            <a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_if_else.asp"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                W3Schools JavaScript If...Else
            </a>
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Example Working Code</h2>

        <label for="myNum01"><b>Enter a number:</b></label>
        <br>

        <input
            id="myNum01"
            type="number"
            value="4"
            step="any"
        >

        <h3>Example 1: Simple If Statement</h3>

        <p>
            If the number is greater than or equal to 3,
            the message will appear.
        </p>

        <button
            class="demo-button"
            type="button"
            onclick="mySimpleIf()">
            Simple If Statement
        </button>

        <h3>Example 2: If...Else Statement</h3>

        <p>
            This checks whether the number is greater than or equal
            to 3. Otherwise, it displays a different message.
        </p>

        <button
            class="demo-button"
            type="button"
            onclick="myIfElse()">
            If...Else
        </button>

        <h3>Example 3: Complex If Statement</h3>

        <p>
            This checks whether the number is not equal to 3,
            or is less than -3, and is also less than or equal to 100.
        </p>

        <button
            class="demo-button"
            type="button"
            onclick="myComplexIf()">
            Complex If
        </button>

        <div class="result" id="myDiv01" aria-live="polite">
            Your result will appear here.
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>What I Learned</h2>

        <ul>
            <li>How to use a simple if statement.</li>
            <li>How to use if...else to choose between two outcomes.</li>
            <li>How to combine conditions using logical operators.</li>
            <li>How to display results with JavaScript and innerHTML.</li>
        </ul>
